# The eval case set is Alan's application history — outcomes, and his own
# candid reasoning about named employers. The repository is public. The store
# is the source of truth and this file is only an export, so nothing is lost
# by keeping it local: `jobagent eval report` still runs and still proves the
# claim. Regenerate it any time with `jobagent eval export`.
evals/cases.yaml

# Outside reviews of this repo. They quote the parts of `profile/` that are
# gitignored for a reason — the salary floor, figures the profile says never to
# publish — alongside candid notes on named employers and response rates. The
# working notes that act on a review belong in the commits; the review itself
# does not belong in a public repository.
REVIEW-*.md
